  "description": "Take an idea, from three words to a short paragraph, through the software delivery cycle (docs/phases.md). The case stores no phase: where it stands is what its facts make true. The root case holds no work of its own. It opens child cases, each worked by another party: sdc.intake (dissection, interview, requirements list), then sdc.direction (project context defaults, vision, roadmap, each approved), then one sdc.epic case per roadmap epic, once the roadmap is approved (ESS specification, AEP plan, stories, release). Every child reports passed when it succeeds. The case ends operating once every epic of the approved roadmap ended passed, or abandoned on an explicit decision; when a child case ended other than passed it ends refused (the intake, before the direction case opened) or not_delivered (any later child), without a person. A revised idea makes intake and direction openable again; a revised roadmap makes its epics openable again.",
  "evidence": [
